{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"agent_message","text":"The disassembly shows `c2Witness` consistently computes `den * weight`, which is already matched. `c2L` is the exception: GCC computes the first weight as `a.u * den` and the second as `den * b.u` because of its argument evaluation/register schedule. I’m applying that one-function asymmetry and rerunning the same seeded stress case."}}
